1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,900
Every day, students walk past broken things on campus — Wi-Fi that drops, heaters that die, railings that wobble.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Reporting means finding the right office, filling out a form, and never hearing back — so most problems just go unreported.

3
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:20,000
We're [NAME], [NAME] and [NAME] — students from WPI, Worcester Polytechnic Institute.

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:26,500
We built UniFix for the Hackachusetts Civic Action challenge V4: better college experiences.

5
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:32,000
Students say what's wrong in plain words, and it goes straight to the one team that can fix it.

6
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:38,000
Here's the student view. A quick pop-up tells judges exactly where they are.

7
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,700
The campus feed shows what's open, what's urgent, and what's already fixed.

8
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,200
The live map shows where problems cluster, colored by severity.

9
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:54,600
Click any bubble to see every report inside it.

10
00:00:54,700 --> 00:01:07,400
First, quality. Spam, jokes, and claims like “I won a million dollars” are blocked before they reach staff — so every report in the queue is real.

11
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,900
But safety beats everything. Ari reads as you type.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:19,200
The moment something sounds like an emergency, UniFix shows Call 911 and campus police — before any AI runs.

13
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,500
Now a real report. Just say what's wrong.

14
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,700
AI picks the team, then asks only what's missing.

15
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,800
Wi-Fi is everywhere — so, no specific place.

16
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:33,900
Ari checks the past: nine similar reports, usually fixed in about three days — plus quick fixes to try first.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,200
Add a photo if you like,

18
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,300
check the card, and post.

19
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:50,100
It's rated Medium and sent to the IT team — and only IT staff can see it. Everyone who co-signs stays in the loop.

20
00:01:50,200 --> 00:02:00,400
On the staff side, each team sees only its own area, ranked by severity times how many students are affected — not by who complains loudest.

21
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:06,700
If something's unclear, staff can message the reporter directly.

22
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:16,700
They can post public updates, then mark it solved. Everyone who co-signed is notified automatically.

23
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:27,100
The student gets a notification. One click opens the conversation, and they answer right there — no emails, no forms, no lost tickets.

24
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,600
A misunderstanding becomes a two-minute chat.

25
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:37,100
We built UniFix with Kiro: specs, steering, hooks, skills and Kiro Crew — backed by over three hundred tests.

26
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:43,100
UniFix works for any Massachusetts campus. Try it yourself — no login needed.
